    "grounding" : {
      "rawText" : "LinkChecker uses the `Executors.newVirtualThreadPerTaskExecutor` factory to create its task executor. This factory creates a new executor service with a single worker thread and a maximum of `Integer.MAX_VALUE` worker threads. The worker threads are created using `ThreadFactory` that creates threads in a non-daemon thread group.\n\nClosing the executor waits for all submitted tasks to finish. This is done by calling the `shutdown` method on the executor service. The `shutdown` method waits for all tasks to complete execution, then it attempts to terminate the thread group, and finally it attempts to stop the thread pool. If any task is actively running, it will be interrupted and a `RejectedExecutionException` will be thrown.\n\nHowever, it's important to note that the `shutdown` method does not wait for actively running tasks to complete. If you need to ensure that all tasks have completed execution, you should use the `awaitTermination` method on the executor service. This method will block until all tasks have completed execution.\n",
